{
  "name": "cloud_sheet_pop",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "A Clear sky turning to rain, which is the instant \u00a725's cloud sheets used to vanish. Three instants are pinned and they are the deterministic ones: the Clear sky before the change, the SAME readings one tick into vanilla's cross-fade, and the settled deck at the far end. THE MIDDLE SET IS THE REGRESSION. On main, cloud_underlight_cover reads 0.0000 one tick in -- CloudFractionFor took \u00a713's blended deck, which is still Clear's own zero at lerp 0 -- so cloud_sheet_alpha gated to 0.0000 and the entire lane stopped drawing, every cloud on the map gone at once, returning one at a time over the following ~400 ticks. Here all five readings are unchanged at that tick and cross-fade to the full deck from there. cloud_sheets_in_view is pinned loosely on purpose: it is the harness's own guard that the camera is actually looking at cloud (a cloudless frame must fail rather than read as a subtle effect), not a measurement of the fix. NOTHING BETWEEN THOSE INSTANTS IS PINNED: FastForward leaves the clock running and overshoots its target by a frame-rate-dependent margin (measured 9-13%), so a mid-transition value is not reproducible between runs. Those captures are there to be looked at. See cloud_drift.json for what happens to the population when the weather does NOT change.",
